\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Solves a constant-coefficient vertical buoyancy balance and proves a transport/diffusivity nonidentifiability from stratification alone.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
The complete supplied definition, including source qualifications and the dated literature assessment, was reviewed. The calculation below is an elementary restricted attempt motivated by [S2]; it does not claim novelty or a fresh literature-status determination.

\paragraph{Context and investigated scope.} The complete supplied definition, including source qualifications and the dated literature assessment, was reviewed. The calculation below is an elementary restricted attempt motivated by [S2]; it does not claim novelty or a fresh literature-status determination.

\paragraph{An exact vertical balance and its ambiguity.} On $0\leq z\leq H$, prescribe constant upward velocity $w$, diffusivity $\kappa>0$, buoyancy endpoints $b(0)=b_0$, $b(H)=b_1$, and steady balance $wb'=\kappa b''$. For $w\ne0$ integration gives
\[
 b(z)=b_0+(b_1-b_0)\frac{e^{wz/\kappa}-1}{e^{wH/\kappa}-1}.
\]
For $w=0$ its continuous limit is the linear profile. Differentiation verifies the equation and endpoints. The stratification $N^2=b'$ is positive when $b_1>b_0$, regardless of the sign of $w$, because numerator and denominator signs cancel.

\paragraph{A concrete identification obstruction.} The profile depends on $w$ and $\kappa$ only through $w/\kappa$. Multiplying both by any $c>0$ leaves $b$ and $N^2$ unchanged while multiplying vertical transport by $c$. Thus stratification data alone cannot identify overturning in this model. Even full knowledge of the profile and boundary values does not resolve the ambiguity without an independent transport or mixing measurement.

\paragraph{Source scope.} The actual source has a basin and a reentrant southern channel, with competing mean and eddy overturning. Its mid-depth stratification cannot be identified with this one-dimensional imposed-upwelling balance without justification. The calculation exposes why an independent closure for eddy compensation, boundary forcing and mixing is needed. Deriving that closure and its basin/channel matching is the first gap; neither a universal ocean formula nor a unique inference of overturning from stratification has been proved.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Checked both signs of w, w=0 limit, stable-gradient sign and exact scaling degeneracy. Model self-audit only; no independent human proof checking. Prompts A and B were applied to this canonical record and its qualified source scope. Checked both signs of w, w=0 limit, stable-gradient sign and exact scaling degeneracy. Retained unresolved status and zero original-target progress; The source basin/channel mean-eddy closure and independent transport information are missing.

Coordinator checked the vertical boundary-value solution, both velocity signs and the common transport/diffusivity scaling ambiguity. This additional check was model-assisted, not independent human verification.

\paragraph{Tools, process and contributions.}
Python 3 was used for file preparation and structural checks; no numerical experiment or theorem prover was used. Contribution prompt A was followed by prompt B. GPT-6 Astra with ultra reasoning drafted the research and performed its stated self-audit; any additional coordinator contribution is identified in the verification and audit. A GPT-6-based Codex coordinator assembled the manuscript and checked repository integration; its exact variant and reasoning configuration were not exposed. No human mathematical contribution, independent human proof check or formal proof certification is supplied. Complete derivations and the consulted source references are included here; private reasoning transcripts are not published.

\paragraph{Final status and first remaining gap.}
\textbf{UNRESOLVED}. The source basin/channel mean-eddy closure and independent transport information are missing.

